Context
  Asked for a baseline of the logs taken before a run, referenced off the project
  directory, so a build check has something to compare against -- prompted by the
  guile3/guile-3.0 naming checks and the hooks documentation.

Deviations
  The request named CLAUDE_PROJECT_ROOT. That variable does not exist; the real one
  is CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, confirmed against the CLI binary. Used the real one and
  recorded the check in the script header so the next reader does not repeat it.

  The baseline records the resolved interpreter and version as well as the log sizes,
  because a session that starts with guile3 3.0.10 and later resolves bare guile 2.2.7
  after a PATH change would otherwise look like a code change.

Considerations
  A hook must never fail a session, so every failure path here exits 0. That is
  deliberate and it is also a limitation: a baseline that could not be written is
  indistinguishable from one that was not needed. The --show mode is the only way to
  tell.

  Not verified: that a SessionStart hook actually fires with this plugin loaded.
  SessionStart exists in the CLI binary and validate accepts the entry, but observing
  it needs a real session (gmake try / try-clean).

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, Claude Code 2.1.261, as
  dsp-dr. gmake checks green; both baseline directions calibrated.
